<BaseLayout title="Tools" description="Bring the design reference into your AI assistant, work through the principles with your team, and explore the Foundation reference app.">
 <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/building-tools/tools.css" />
 <div class="tools-wrap">
  <header class="tools-intro"><h1>Put the principles<br />to work.</h1><div><p class="tools-lead">Tools for the decisions your team is making.</p><p>Bring the reference into your assistant, examine a feature together, or explore how the principles inform a working app.</p></div></header>
  <nav class="tool-rows" aria-label="Choose a building tool">
   <article><h2><a href="/bezalel/">Bezalel MCP</a></h2><div><p>Bring theological reflection into everyday faith-app design. Bezalel connects principles with real app patterns and source-linked research in your AI assistant—helping you examine what a feature teaches, how it shapes spiritual practice and what to change.</p><p class="tool-state">Available · hosted connector, desktop bundle and skill</p></div><a class="tool-action" href="/bezalel/#add">Connect your assistant</a></article>
   <article><h2><a href="/building-tools/worksheet/">Principle worksheet</a></h2><div><p>Take one feature through the ten principle questions. Record what you know, whose experience is missing and what your team will test next.</p><p class="tool-state">Available · fill in and print · no account</p></div><a class="tool-action" href="/building-tools/worksheet/">Start a team review</a></article>
   <article><h2><a href="#foundation">Foundation app</a></h2><div><p>A reference app and reusable capabilities for Bible reading and source-aware study conversations. See the choices being explored and where review is still needed.</p><p class="tool-state">In development · collaboration and review welcome</p></div><a class="tool-action" href="#foundation">Explore the work</a></article>
  </nav>
  <section class="tools-support" aria-labelledby="team-tools"><h2 id="team-tools">Start with your context.</h2><p>For a broader conversation about whom you serve and what good news means here, use the <a href="/missional-canvas/">missional canvas</a>. For one concrete feature, the <a href="/guides/decision-review/">decision-review worksheet</a> helps compare alternatives. Both complement the principle review.</p></section>
  <section id="foundation" class="foundation-section" aria-labelledby="foundation-title">
   <div class="foundation-copy"><h2 id="foundation-title">From principles<br />to a working app.</h2><p>The Faith App Foundation is our development project for shared Bible and faith-app capabilities. Its reference journey connects reading a passage, consulting sources and asking a study question.</p><p>The current work includes Bible-source connectors, a reference reader and study-chat implementation. Device checks and safeguarding review remain open. It is work in development, with no general public app or platform release offered here.</p><p>The intended model combines a free, open safety layer with a licensed platform. Package separation, release terms and review work remain to be completed before public distribution.</p><p><EmailLink label="Discuss collaboration or a review" class="tool-action" /></p></div>
   <figure class="foundation-figure"><div class="foundation-screens"><a href="/assets/building-tools/foundation-reader.webp"><img src="/assets/building-tools/foundation-reader.webp" width="780" height="1688" alt="Foundation reference app reader, showing Luke 15 with the Bible edition and editorial-heading attribution." loading="lazy" /></a><a href="/assets/building-tools/foundation-study-chat.webp"><img src="/assets/building-tools/foundation-study-chat.webp" width="780" height="1688" alt="Foundation study-chat prototype, separating the assistant response from a labelled Scripture passage." loading="lazy" /></a></div><figcaption>Our own reference-app prototypes. The chat answer is synthetic demonstration content, not a live-answer evaluation. These screens retain their app’s own appearance.</figcaption></figure>
  </section>
  <section class="tools-support"><h2>Research and building, in conversation.</h2><p>Missional by Design is an independent research and design resource by Tobias Treppmann. The Foundation is our own implementation work, not an independent market example. We keep observations, proposals and product demonstrations distinct; collaboration or payment does not change an app assessment.</p><p><a href="/apps/assessment/">Read the assessment method</a> · <a href="/feedback/">Offer a correction or another perspective</a></p></section>
 </div>
</BaseLayout>
